WEBVTT

00:06.861 --> 00:08.111
♪

00:08.611 --> 00:10.531
[ÖGEDEI]
Thanks to your lovely earrings,

00:10.611 --> 00:13.701
I have learned that all
is functioning as it should.

00:18.961 --> 00:20.331
[Möge breathes softly]

00:20.411 --> 00:22.171
[ÖGEDEI]
I have to wonder, though...

00:22.791 --> 00:24.751
Will people come
to see it my way

00:24.881 --> 00:27.001
after we have defeated
all the Jin?

00:33.601 --> 00:37.511
[MÖGE] <i>Honestly, I don't have</i>
<i>any idea what he's thinking.</i>

00:38.311 --> 00:39.271
Hm?

00:39.351 --> 00:42.021
[gasps] The slave girl's gone?

00:42.101 --> 00:43.021
Ah!

00:43.731 --> 00:44.771
[exclaims]

00:45.151 --> 00:47.861
Ugh, did she get lost again?

00:48.031 --> 00:49.781
Lady Möge!

00:51.071 --> 00:53.741
[♪ opening theme song playing]

01:01.411 --> 01:03.581
JAADUGAR

02:26.121 --> 02:27.961
[Qadaq grunts]

02:28.671 --> 02:31.171
-Hey, Fatima.
-[Sitara gasps, sighs]

02:31.251 --> 02:33.301
-So this is where you were.
-[gasps softly]

02:34.091 --> 02:36.381
-How dare you run away!
-[Sitara squeals]

02:36.471 --> 02:39.391
Qadaq! You have to help me.

02:39.471 --> 02:40.851
[BOTH] Lord Chinqai?

02:40.931 --> 02:43.391
You can write in Uyghur, right?

02:43.521 --> 02:44.811
[both gasp]

02:44.891 --> 02:46.481
♪

02:49.521 --> 02:50.771
[MAN]
Take care of these as well.

02:50.861 --> 02:53.071
Uh... there's no end in sight.

02:53.691 --> 02:54.991
I'm sorry about this.

02:55.491 --> 02:57.951
Every item
the Great Kha'an purchased

02:58.031 --> 03:00.241
has to be recorded
in our registers.

03:01.371 --> 03:02.911
So why am I here?

03:03.041 --> 03:05.251
Isn't this considered
a man's job?

03:05.331 --> 03:07.121
Just be quiet and get to work.

03:07.211 --> 03:10.081
Many Mongols have never
really had a strong affinity

03:10.171 --> 03:11.591
for reading and writing.

03:11.671 --> 03:14.011
Thus we're short on scribes.

03:14.091 --> 03:15.301
[Sitara gasps] Books!

03:15.381 --> 03:16.591
[both laugh]

03:16.721 --> 03:18.261
Who'll even read these?

03:19.051 --> 03:21.301
This one is by Jabir ibn Hayyan.

03:21.391 --> 03:24.271
-Huh?
-Uh... Oh, nothing.

03:24.431 --> 03:26.351
♪

03:29.941 --> 03:30.861
[Sitara gasps]

03:30.941 --> 03:34.611
Mistress, why is this book
hidden away among the others?

03:35.401 --> 03:39.911
Oh, you have quite a keen eye.
This one's by Jabir.

03:39.991 --> 03:41.871
He lived in Tus long ago.

03:42.911 --> 03:45.911
But I'm afraid it's not
the most reputable of tomes.

03:46.961 --> 03:48.421
What's the subject of his book?

03:50.871 --> 03:53.341
[chuckles] It's alchemy.

03:54.381 --> 03:55.961
[Sitara gasps]

03:57.211 --> 03:58.421
What's that about?

03:59.011 --> 04:00.551
[SITARA]
<i>It details how one can heat</i>

04:00.641 --> 04:02.261
<i>and mix various substances,</i>

04:02.341 --> 04:04.261
<i>such as minerals,</i>
<i>to prepare.</i>..

04:05.061 --> 04:06.221
<i>an al-iksir.</i>

04:06.981 --> 04:08.561
An "al-iksir"?

04:08.641 --> 04:09.811
And what is that?

04:09.891 --> 04:11.311
It's a kind of cure-all,

04:11.401 --> 04:13.111
at least I think
that's what it is.

04:13.521 --> 04:14.861
I'm not quite sure.

04:15.321 --> 04:16.901
-[MÖGE] A cure-all?
-[ALL] Huh?

04:17.691 --> 04:18.821
[SITARA] Lady Möge!

04:18.951 --> 04:21.741
Do you mean a medicine
that can cure any ailment?

04:21.821 --> 04:22.991
[Sitara whimpers]

04:23.121 --> 04:24.031
Huh?

04:26.911 --> 04:28.251
[TÖREGENE] This is Fatima.

04:28.331 --> 04:30.791
She is one
of my most faithful attendants,

04:30.871 --> 04:32.631
Boraqchin Khatun.

04:34.251 --> 04:36.001
[SITARA]
<i>So this is the chief empress</i>

04:36.091 --> 04:37.211
<i>of the Mongol Empire...</i>

04:38.631 --> 04:40.051
<i>The Great Khatun.</i>

04:40.921 --> 04:43.681
<i>Why have I been brought out here</i>
<i>to meet her like this?</i>

04:44.011 --> 04:46.601
Listen, Boraqchin,
this girl here says

04:46.681 --> 04:48.141
that she is able
to concoct a cure-all.

04:48.931 --> 04:50.061
A danyao?

04:50.141 --> 04:51.231
Huh?

04:51.441 --> 04:55.941
I, uh... I'm sorry, but I'm
not sure what this is about,

04:56.481 --> 04:57.781
because all I said

04:57.861 --> 05:00.531
is that I'm able to read books
written in Arabic.

05:01.151 --> 05:03.071
-[MÖGE] You what?
-Möge.

05:03.161 --> 05:04.531
[MÖGE] Uh, but...

05:04.701 --> 05:07.031
-That is all. Take your leave.
-[Möge groans]

05:07.621 --> 05:09.911
[BORAQCHIN]
Sorry for making you come here.

05:10.501 --> 05:11.871
[sheep bleating]

05:13.211 --> 05:15.251
So what was all of that about?

05:15.331 --> 05:16.541
Who knows?

05:17.421 --> 05:18.881
-[MÖGE] Hold on!
-[BOTH] Uh?

05:18.961 --> 05:20.091
[SITARA] Lady Möge?

05:20.171 --> 05:23.051
[MÖGE] Say, there's something
I wanted to discuss with you.

05:23.551 --> 05:26.641
The whole reason I asked you
to come out here. [sighs]

05:27.761 --> 05:29.181
Please leave us.

05:29.271 --> 05:31.271
[birds chirping]

05:32.771 --> 05:34.561
[MÖGE] Someone's been
administering poison

05:34.651 --> 05:36.361
-to Boraqchin.
-[Sitara gasps]

05:36.441 --> 05:38.071
[MÖGE] You could see
how emaciated she was,

05:38.151 --> 05:40.031
and all the sores
all over her skin.

05:40.111 --> 05:43.241
Who did this?
Why would they do such a thing?

05:43.821 --> 05:46.451
[MÖGE] I'm not certain,
and I can't prove it.

05:47.031 --> 05:49.661
But I think the culprit
is Boraqchin's physician.

05:50.251 --> 05:52.961
Some time ago,
the Daoists engaged

05:53.041 --> 05:55.171
in a sacred tradition
known as waidan.

05:55.711 --> 05:56.881
What's waidan?

05:56.961 --> 05:59.211
[PHYSICIAN] <i>By combining</i>
<i>the likes of sulfur,</i>

05:59.341 --> 06:01.261
<i>quicksilver, and sandarac,</i>

06:01.341 --> 06:04.091
<i>an elixir called</i>
<i>"danyao" can be created.</i>

06:04.171 --> 06:06.971
<i>It was believed</i>
<i>that after ingesting danyao,</i>

06:07.051 --> 06:10.851
<i>one's body would transform</i>
<i>and become immortal like gold.</i>

06:10.931 --> 06:12.141
Was it really true?

06:12.271 --> 06:13.351
Sadly, no.

06:13.891 --> 06:16.191
Many of the ingredients
were highly poisonous,

06:16.271 --> 06:18.111
shortening the lives
of all who used it.

06:18.651 --> 06:19.901
For that reason,

06:19.981 --> 06:22.861
this archaic practice
was abandoned centuries ago.

06:23.361 --> 06:24.611
He said poison.

06:24.701 --> 06:26.491
I'm sure that's the word
I heard him utter.

06:26.571 --> 06:29.081
Unfortunately,
it isn't much to go on.

06:29.161 --> 06:32.201
If it worries you so,
simply keep the physician away.

06:32.291 --> 06:33.621
As Great Khatun,

06:33.711 --> 06:36.121
surely it would be simple
to replace him.

06:36.501 --> 06:37.501
Töregene.

06:37.581 --> 06:39.381
[TÖREGENE]
Let us return, Fatima.

06:39.461 --> 06:40.591
[SITARA] Um, right.

06:41.761 --> 06:43.011
[exhales softly]

06:44.761 --> 06:46.341
[insects trilling]

06:47.221 --> 06:49.051
[TÖREGENE] Neither one of us
should get involved

06:49.141 --> 06:50.601
with such an eerie woman.

06:50.681 --> 06:53.061
[sighs deeply] How harrowing.

06:53.971 --> 06:56.231
This was the first time
I'd seen the Great Khatun,

06:56.311 --> 06:57.521
and I couldn't help noticing

06:57.601 --> 07:00.401
she's considerably older
than Emperor Ögedei.

07:00.521 --> 07:02.861
You're right. She used
to be his stepmother.

07:02.941 --> 07:03.901
Huh?

07:03.981 --> 07:05.201
[TÖREGENE] <i>Years ago,</i>

07:05.281 --> 07:08.161
<i>Boraqchin and Möge</i>
<i>were married to Genghis Khan,</i>

07:08.281 --> 07:10.831
<i>then Ögedei inherited them</i>
<i>as wives.</i>

07:10.911 --> 07:11.831
[Sitara gasps]

07:12.451 --> 07:14.041
So the two of them
have known each other

07:14.121 --> 07:15.621
for quite a long time then.

07:15.911 --> 07:17.291
When the father dies,

07:17.371 --> 07:20.671
all his wives go to his son,
except for the birth mother.

07:21.131 --> 07:23.341
It's a common arrangement here.

07:24.131 --> 07:25.211
[Töregene sighs]

07:26.631 --> 07:28.131
Boraqchin...

07:28.511 --> 07:30.341
[coughing]

07:30.841 --> 07:32.261
[TÖREGENE] <i>She has no sons,</i>

07:32.351 --> 07:34.891
<i>and she doesn't come</i>
<i>from a large family.</i>

07:35.311 --> 07:36.811
<i>Truth be told,</i>

07:36.941 --> 07:40.231
<i>I don't have any idea</i>
<i>how she became Great Khatun.</i>

07:43.231 --> 07:46.031
[PHYSICIAN] <i>It was believed</i>
<i>that after ingesting danyao,</i>

07:46.151 --> 07:50.241
<i>one's body would transform</i>
<i>and become immortal like gold.</i>

07:50.321 --> 07:52.411
That sounds
exactly like alchemy.

07:52.491 --> 07:53.581
Who knew they had

07:53.661 --> 07:55.251
something so similar
in the east?

07:56.501 --> 07:58.211
An immortal body.

07:59.081 --> 08:00.171
A danyao?

08:01.291 --> 08:02.381
[Sitara gasps]

08:04.171 --> 08:07.591
I wonder if it's... an al-iksir.

08:08.671 --> 08:12.641
The ingredients
are quicksilver, sulfur...

08:13.261 --> 08:15.931
And what were
the other substances again?

08:17.811 --> 08:18.731
[rustling]

08:18.811 --> 08:20.231
-[SITARA] Lady Töregene.
-Huh?

08:20.851 --> 08:23.651
Once more, let's go meet
with the Great Khatun.

08:23.731 --> 08:26.361
Huh? Why is that?

08:26.941 --> 08:28.031
[Sitara chuckles softly]

08:28.651 --> 08:29.781
[Töregene grunts]

08:30.701 --> 08:32.491
You have something
in mind, don't you?

08:33.121 --> 08:34.201
Mm-hmm.

08:35.081 --> 08:36.911
I'd like you
to lend me your power.

08:37.001 --> 08:38.451
Please, Lady Töregene.

08:40.501 --> 08:41.671
[birds chirping]

08:42.711 --> 08:43.961
[SITARA] Al-iksir.

08:44.591 --> 08:47.091
It's a remedy
that renders one immortal.

08:47.631 --> 08:48.841
For generations now,

08:48.921 --> 08:51.511
it's lain at the very heart
of Persian alchemy.

08:51.591 --> 08:53.011
-[Möge gasps]
-[SITARA] Of course,

08:53.141 --> 08:55.721
I cannot prepare
such a thing by myself.

08:56.351 --> 08:59.431
That said, if you were to
assist me, Great Khatun,

09:00.021 --> 09:01.271
I could.

09:01.901 --> 09:03.611
Why is there talk of this again?

09:03.691 --> 09:07.071
Because I believe
it's you who's been seeking it.

09:08.071 --> 09:09.151
Am I wrong?

09:09.611 --> 09:10.531
[Boraqchin grunts]

09:10.611 --> 09:12.241
Wait. Is that really true?

09:13.161 --> 09:14.951
From the moment I laid eyes
on you,

09:15.031 --> 09:16.201
there was something
that struck me.

09:16.281 --> 09:19.581
If I may surmise,
based on your appearance...

09:20.581 --> 09:23.791
Have you been ingesting
rahj al-gar by any chance?

09:23.881 --> 09:26.251
[MÖGE] What's rahj al-gar?

09:27.251 --> 09:28.591
[SITARA] <i>It's a red stone</i>

09:28.671 --> 09:30.471
<i>that can be found</i>
<i>in volcanoes</i>.

09:30.551 --> 09:31.591
<i>And in the east,</i>

09:31.671 --> 09:33.891
<i>I've been told they refer to it</i>
<i>as "sandarac."</i>

09:33.971 --> 09:34.931
[Boraqchin gasps]

09:35.011 --> 09:36.551
So I was right.

09:37.011 --> 09:39.061
In al-iksir and danyao,

09:39.141 --> 09:40.431
rahj al-gar is regarded

09:40.521 --> 09:42.811
as an essential ingredient,
after all.

09:43.651 --> 09:45.151
According
to the ancient physician

09:45.231 --> 09:46.731
named Hippocrates,

09:46.811 --> 09:49.111
rahj al-gar does have
medicinal effects

09:49.191 --> 09:50.821
in small doses.

09:50.941 --> 09:54.451
Although, it's poisonous
with continued use,

09:54.531 --> 09:56.411
causing loss of appetite,

09:56.491 --> 09:59.331
lesions on the skin,
and the growth of tumors,

09:59.951 --> 10:02.791
which is what you
seem to be suffering from.

10:02.871 --> 10:05.331
So my fear that you were
slowly being poisoned

10:05.421 --> 10:06.711
is completely unfounded,

10:06.841 --> 10:08.671
and you chose
to ingest it yourself?

10:08.751 --> 10:10.511
Goodness, Möge.

10:10.631 --> 10:12.881
Is that honestly
what you were thinking?

10:13.381 --> 10:14.841
Fatima, right?

10:14.931 --> 10:17.931
You should take a look inside
the drawers on that shelf.

10:21.181 --> 10:22.771
There's the rahj al-gar.

10:22.851 --> 10:25.231
Why were you taking
such a harmful thing?

10:25.851 --> 10:26.981
[Boraqchin sighs]

10:29.611 --> 10:32.191
To become immortal. Was that it?

10:33.241 --> 10:34.191
[Boraqchin grunts]

10:35.361 --> 10:36.321
[MÖGE] Huh?

10:36.411 --> 10:39.831
Yes, that's right.
I'm not a young woman anymore.

10:40.411 --> 10:42.161
I'd like to live a long life.

10:42.251 --> 10:43.541
Mistress Boraqchin.

10:44.121 --> 10:47.001
[SITARA] If you wouldn't mind,
please ingest this.

10:47.671 --> 10:49.671
Its medicine will cure you.

10:50.341 --> 10:51.381
[ALL] Huh?

10:53.301 --> 10:54.341
[breathes softly]

11:01.601 --> 11:03.731
Tell me, what is this?

11:03.811 --> 11:06.271
-A Jada stone.
-Jada stone?

11:06.351 --> 11:08.941
I thought you were not supposed
to ingest Jada stones.

11:09.021 --> 11:12.571
You're wrong. It's called
a bezoar stone in Persia,

11:12.691 --> 11:14.651
where it has been recognized
as an antidote.

11:15.191 --> 11:17.611
I assume you haven't put a curse
on this, right?

11:17.701 --> 11:20.161
Is this the face of someone
who wishes you ill?

11:20.281 --> 11:21.201
[Töregene groans]

11:21.281 --> 11:22.281
[BORAQCHIN] Hm.

11:30.381 --> 11:31.841
[Boraqchin coughs]

11:32.671 --> 11:35.051
After you've recovered
and are feeling better,

11:35.131 --> 11:36.511
please summon us here again.

11:37.551 --> 11:41.011
We'll talk more
of the al-iksir, if you wish.

11:44.021 --> 11:45.851
[SITARA]
Thank you very much.

11:45.931 --> 11:47.851
[TÖREGENE]
But I haven't done anything.

11:47.941 --> 11:48.851
[SITARA] Of course you have.

11:49.601 --> 11:51.111
<i>If you hadn't been able to find</i>

11:51.191 --> 11:53.441
<i>those Persian physicians</i>
<i>who spoke with us,</i>

11:53.571 --> 11:56.361
<i>I never would have learned</i>
<i>about the rahj al-gar.</i>

11:57.651 --> 11:59.661
[TÖREGENE]
What'll you do about Chagatai?

11:59.741 --> 12:01.411
[SITARA] I think we may
have been rushing things

12:01.491 --> 12:03.661
by assuming we should
approach him right away.

12:04.491 --> 12:05.911
At this point,

12:06.001 --> 12:08.871
by just focusing on earning
the Great Khatun's trust,

12:09.371 --> 12:11.461
a path will reveal itself.

12:11.841 --> 12:14.251
One for us both, I hope.

12:15.131 --> 12:16.301
Yes.

12:17.171 --> 12:18.551
Absolutely.

12:20.301 --> 12:22.851
SUMMER, A.D. 1230

12:27.891 --> 12:29.271
[SITARA (ADULT)]
<i>Shortly thereafter,</i>

12:30.021 --> 12:32.811
<i>the Mongol Emperor</i>
<i>embarked on an expedition</i>

12:32.901 --> 12:34.771
<i>against the Jin dynasty.</i>

12:40.531 --> 12:43.621
SHANXI REGION - HOUSE OF ÖGEDEI
FRONT-LINE CAMP

12:46.241 --> 12:49.161
You can put those
right over there for now.

12:49.291 --> 12:51.421
-[BORAQCHIN] Möge.
-[both gasp]

12:51.501 --> 12:52.831
[MÖGE] Boraqchin!

12:52.921 --> 12:54.211
-[Kirgistani exclaims]
-You're well enough

12:54.291 --> 12:56.381
to be walking outside?
[chuckles]

12:56.501 --> 12:58.591
-Yes, so it seems.
-[Kirgistani exclaims]

12:58.671 --> 13:00.921
-It's all thanks to Fatima.
-Yeah!

13:02.091 --> 13:03.471
[BORAQCHIN] Indeed.

13:04.891 --> 13:07.891
[ATTENDANT] <i>I have a message</i>
<i>from Empress Boraqchin.</i>

13:07.971 --> 13:11.101
She's requested that Miss Fatima
come speak with her again.

13:12.731 --> 13:13.651
[Sitara grunts]

13:14.231 --> 13:15.191
[Töregene exhales]

13:15.311 --> 13:16.361
[SITARA (ADULT)]
<i>The following year</i>...

13:16.441 --> 13:17.611
MONGOLS - SOUTHERN SONG
KAIFENG JIN DYNASTY

13:17.691 --> 13:19.571
<i>to ensure</i>
<i>the Jin capital of Kaifeng</i>

13:19.651 --> 13:21.321
<i>would be</i>
<i>completely surrounded,</i>

13:21.491 --> 13:23.161
<i>Tolui's army sought permission</i>

13:23.241 --> 13:25.661
<i>to pass through the lands</i>
<i>of the Southern Song</i>.

13:25.741 --> 13:26.781
<i>But instead...</i>

13:27.831 --> 13:29.451
They killed our messenger?

13:30.081 --> 13:32.251
So that's the Southern Song's
response.

13:32.921 --> 13:34.211
Should we all turn back?

13:35.791 --> 13:36.841
Hardly.

13:36.921 --> 13:39.461
We'll proceed south
exactly as we planned.

13:39.551 --> 13:42.761
We've already received
their unfavorable reply.

13:43.181 --> 13:47.181
If we go, none of their people
will take this quietly.

13:48.431 --> 13:50.141
[Tolui scoffs] Well...

13:51.061 --> 13:53.441
we'll just have
to defeat them too.

13:53.941 --> 13:55.311
[soldiers shouting]

13:59.021 --> 14:00.111
[groans]

14:04.451 --> 14:06.071
[all grunting]

14:11.451 --> 14:14.581
[SITARA (ADULT)] <i>Tolui's army</i>
<i>breached the fortified pass,</i>

14:14.711 --> 14:17.461
<i>then continued along</i>
<i>the mountain roads.</i>

14:19.421 --> 14:22.921
[TOLUI] These mountains prove
to be no match for us after all.

14:24.381 --> 14:26.891
The Great Kha'an
will be most pleased.

14:26.971 --> 14:27.891
Huh?

14:29.261 --> 14:31.061
Without question.

14:31.851 --> 14:34.851
I have no doubt my brother
will be overjoyed!

14:34.941 --> 14:37.981
[laughs]

14:38.061 --> 14:39.731
[sheep bleating]

14:44.151 --> 14:45.491
[SORGHAGHTANI] Dear God,

14:46.071 --> 14:48.781
please bless Tolui
and watch over him.

14:49.371 --> 14:52.501
[HULEGU] Come now, you know
Father would never lose.

14:52.581 --> 14:53.701
TOLUI'S SON
HULEGU

14:53.791 --> 14:55.411
Why even bother praying for him?

14:55.501 --> 14:58.591
My! How could you say that
before God?

14:59.341 --> 15:01.301
I feel confident
that my dear husband

15:01.381 --> 15:02.921
would never lose in battle.

15:03.471 --> 15:04.551
That said,

15:04.921 --> 15:08.431
misfortune can strike
outside of the battlefield.

15:08.511 --> 15:10.391
Those with too much power

15:10.471 --> 15:12.891
are viewed with great fear
and resentment.

15:13.021 --> 15:15.431
Mother, then you
must be careful too.

15:15.891 --> 15:18.191
I must be? [giggles]

15:18.271 --> 15:21.271
No one would give me
any thought whatsoever.

15:24.651 --> 15:26.361
[HULEGU] I can only hope so.

15:28.161 --> 15:30.491
[sheep bleating]

15:30.621 --> 15:32.241
♪

15:38.541 --> 15:39.581
[Sitara grunts]

15:40.501 --> 15:41.841
[bells jingle]

15:45.301 --> 15:46.881
Here you are. [grunts]

15:47.051 --> 15:48.721
Thank you. Right there is fine.

15:48.801 --> 15:50.721
♪

16:07.151 --> 16:08.991
There, fresh off the pot.

16:09.411 --> 16:11.161
Thank you very much.

16:11.821 --> 16:14.621
I thought I'd bring you
some urum, Lady Töregene.

16:15.411 --> 16:17.541
[exclaims]
I love it the most now

16:17.621 --> 16:19.371
when it's at its ripest.

16:20.631 --> 16:21.841
[chuckles]

16:22.461 --> 16:24.091
So good.

16:24.171 --> 16:26.261
Autumn will soon be upon us,

16:26.381 --> 16:28.631
and the urum will be used
to make butter.

16:29.011 --> 16:30.971
This may be the last batch
of the season.

16:31.051 --> 16:32.971
You should have some as well.

16:33.051 --> 16:34.351
Oh, I couldn't.

16:34.431 --> 16:38.101
Besides, Empress Boraqchin
has just asked to speak with me.

16:38.181 --> 16:39.521
What, again?

16:39.601 --> 16:42.191
I'm sorry.
I should be going now.

16:42.271 --> 16:43.441
[Töregene sighs]

16:43.521 --> 16:44.771
♪

16:54.371 --> 16:56.581
That's all right by me.

17:00.041 --> 17:01.831
[SITARA]
In the natural world,

17:01.921 --> 17:04.921
substance and qualities
are very closely intermingled.

17:05.001 --> 17:07.551
By altering
its essential properties,

17:07.671 --> 17:10.631
one thing can be entirely
transformed into another.

17:11.181 --> 17:12.931
In much simpler terms,

17:13.011 --> 17:15.721
that is what this treatise
by Jabir is really all about.

17:16.511 --> 17:17.681
What does it mean?

17:17.771 --> 17:19.891
[BORAQCHIN] By understanding
an object's qualities,

17:19.981 --> 17:22.021
one can make whatever
is desired,

17:22.101 --> 17:24.021
whether that be a remedy
or a weapon.

17:24.151 --> 17:25.611
Oh, wow, amazing!

17:25.691 --> 17:27.611
Just look at sandarac.

17:27.691 --> 17:29.361
When rahj al-gar is heated,

17:29.441 --> 17:32.401
it immediately turns white
and becomes more toxic.

17:32.911 --> 17:35.451
They seem to have approached
the truth of this world,

17:35.531 --> 17:37.581
both, the scholars
of your homeland,

17:37.701 --> 17:39.621
and Daoists
of the Middle Kingdom.

17:40.041 --> 17:41.541
[Sitara gasps]

17:42.661 --> 17:45.591
[SITARA] <i>The Great Kha'an</i>
<i>and Empress Boraqchin,</i>

17:45.751 --> 17:47.051
<i>they're thinking about</i>
<i>what happens</i>

17:47.131 --> 17:49.091
<i>after the Jin</i>
<i>have been conquered.</i>

17:49.591 --> 17:52.261
<i>And they're taking</i>
<i>a broader view of the world.</i>

17:53.431 --> 17:54.341
Uh...

17:55.101 --> 17:56.051
[Sitara sighs]

17:56.141 --> 17:58.261
What's the matter?
Are you all right?

17:58.721 --> 18:01.351
[SITARA] Uh, well,
Lord Chinqai mentioned

18:01.431 --> 18:02.891
that he was struggling
with the shortage

18:02.981 --> 18:04.231
of scribes here.

18:05.151 --> 18:07.361
But I don't understand
how that could be.

18:07.441 --> 18:09.481
Haven't the Mongols
obtained people and knowledge

18:09.571 --> 18:10.981
from all over the world?

18:11.071 --> 18:12.741
-[BORAQCHIN] Mm.
-[MÖGE] Hm?

18:12.901 --> 18:15.121
The Mongols
have obtained intellectuals,

18:15.201 --> 18:16.991
but a great vast majority
of them...

18:17.491 --> 18:20.041
<i>fall under</i>
<i>the House of Tolui's rule now.</i>

18:20.121 --> 18:21.291
[Sitara gasps]

18:21.371 --> 18:22.661
Just like the military,

18:22.751 --> 18:25.331
Prince Tolui is entitled
as Otchigin.

18:25.461 --> 18:27.591
If that's true,
then couldn't the Great Kha'an

18:27.671 --> 18:29.341
just use his authority?

18:29.501 --> 18:30.501
Are you suggesting

18:30.591 --> 18:32.671
that he should pilfer
his own brother's property?

18:32.761 --> 18:34.931
I... I am sorry.

18:35.971 --> 18:38.601
<i>There's an intellectual</i>
<i>imbalance as well?</i>

18:39.721 --> 18:42.561
<i>Actually, that should work</i>
<i>to our advantage.</i>

18:43.931 --> 18:46.731
Do you truly believe
that would be for the best?

18:46.861 --> 18:47.771
[BOTH] Huh?

18:48.691 --> 18:50.861
[SITARA]
I can't help but feel afraid.

18:51.031 --> 18:54.611
The House of Tolui controls
military and intellectual might.

18:55.451 --> 18:56.991
Well, that only means...

18:57.071 --> 18:58.531
...that it is
even more important

18:58.621 --> 19:00.331
to work in tandem with them.
[chuckles]

19:02.081 --> 19:04.501
Does Prince Tolui
feel the same way, though?

19:04.581 --> 19:05.791
[MÖGE] Hmm.

19:06.331 --> 19:09.041
[BORAQCHIN] Möge, forgive me,
but could you leave us?

19:09.211 --> 19:10.131
[gasps softly]

19:18.091 --> 19:19.971
Till Möge brought you to us,

19:20.101 --> 19:21.431
I have no recollection

19:21.511 --> 19:23.311
of ever once
having seen you here before.

19:24.021 --> 19:26.101
So who in the world are you?

19:27.401 --> 19:29.361
[SITARA] I'm sure you wouldn't
be familiar with me.

19:32.401 --> 19:35.991
After all, I was serving
as Princess Sorghaghtani's aide.

19:36.991 --> 19:38.911
I urge you to be cautious.

19:38.991 --> 19:40.951
She hasn't given up
on her ambition...

19:41.451 --> 19:44.581
to see Prince Tolui
become the Great Kha'an

19:44.661 --> 19:46.961
and for herself
to be the Great Khatun.

19:48.211 --> 19:49.421
[Boraqchin gasps]

19:50.711 --> 19:52.631
Sorghaghtani, you say?

19:54.801 --> 19:58.261
I see. I shall bear it
in mind then.

19:59.141 --> 20:01.051
But why have you suddenly chosen

20:01.141 --> 20:03.721
to divulge all this
to me, Fatima?

20:04.261 --> 20:07.181
I must warn you
to choose your answer wisely.

20:07.941 --> 20:10.361
[SITARA] <i>It's all right.</i>
<i>I can do this.</i>

20:10.441 --> 20:11.521
<i>As of now,</i>

20:11.611 --> 20:14.611
<i>I have a fairly good sense</i>
<i>of what's going on in her mind.</i>

20:15.731 --> 20:17.241
Truth be told,

20:17.361 --> 20:20.201
I don't have any idea
how she became Great Khatun.

20:21.241 --> 20:23.621
[SITARA] <i>No matter how wise</i>
<i>this woman is,</i>

20:23.701 --> 20:26.451
<i>there must be many who think</i>
<i>as Lady Töregene does.</i>

20:26.541 --> 20:29.871
<i>People question how she came</i>
<i>to hold such authority,</i>

20:30.331 --> 20:33.211
<i>which is why she clings</i>
<i>so firmly to her own acumen.</i>

20:33.961 --> 20:35.091
Simply put,

20:35.631 --> 20:37.131
you and Emperor Ögedei

20:37.211 --> 20:39.011
have filled me
with a sense of hope!

20:39.091 --> 20:40.011
[Boraqchin exclaims]

20:40.091 --> 20:42.391
[SITARA] The great wisdom
you both display

20:42.471 --> 20:45.471
makes you worthy of ruling
this world with honor and grace.

20:45.561 --> 20:46.471
Yes.

20:46.561 --> 20:47.811
♪

20:47.891 --> 20:49.981
[Boraqchin gasps]

20:51.981 --> 20:54.651
Do you really think so?

20:58.151 --> 20:59.951
Of course I do.

21:00.031 --> 21:01.951
[footsteps]

21:02.031 --> 21:04.741
[SITARA] <i>I expected her</i>
<i>to be a fairly crafty one,</i>

21:04.831 --> 21:06.791
<i>but she was so easy to handle.</i>

21:06.911 --> 21:09.331
<i>I have to tell Lady Töregene</i>
<i>about this.</i>

21:09.411 --> 21:11.421
-[FEMALE SLAVE] Excuse me!
-Uh?

21:11.501 --> 21:15.381
[pants] Um, I was attempting
to make butter,

21:15.501 --> 21:17.501
but I'm still not used to it,

21:17.711 --> 21:21.011
and I have plenty of milk.
You see, it's over there.

21:21.631 --> 21:23.471
I'd be glad to help.
Don't worry.

21:24.011 --> 21:26.431
[exclaims]
Thank you so very much.

21:26.601 --> 21:27.721
[female slave chuckles]

21:28.311 --> 21:30.851
Oh, Lady Töregene.

21:32.691 --> 21:33.941
Guess it can wait.

21:36.781 --> 21:38.361
[footsteps]

21:46.281 --> 21:48.291
[SITARA] Lady Töregene?

21:52.411 --> 21:53.831
[BORAQCHIN]
There's no need for you

21:53.921 --> 21:55.591
to feel so nervous.

21:56.421 --> 21:59.631
I just have something I wanted
to discuss with you.

22:04.091 --> 22:08.011
GREAT KHATUN BORAQCHIN

22:08.101 --> 22:11.311
[♪ closing theme song playing]

23:39.151 --> 23:41.361
[SITARA (ADULT)]
<i>Next time. "Tengri."</i>

23:41.481 --> 23:42.941
TENGRI
